# MQTT Remote Terminal

A lightweight remote terminal system that lets you control an **STM32MP1** (or any ARM Linux board) from your PC over MQTT — no SSH, no VPN, just a broker in the middle.

```
┌─────────────┐        MQTT / TLS        ┌──────────────────┐
│  Your PC    │  ──────────────────────► │  HiveMQ Cloud    │
│  (Python)   │  ◄──────────────────────  │  Broker          │
└─────────────┘                          └────────┬─────────┘
                                                  │
                                         ┌────────▼─────────┐
                                         │  STM32MP1 Board  │
                                         │  (C agent)       │
                                         └──────────────────┘
```

---

## Project Structure

```
mqtt-terminal/
├── pi_terminal_agent.c   # C agent — runs on the STM32MP1 board
├── cJSON.c               # Bundled JSON library (no install needed)
├── cJSON.h
└── mqtt_terminal.py      # Python terminal client — runs on your PC
```

---

## Board Agent (`pi_terminal_agent.c`)

### What it does
- Connects to HiveMQ Cloud over **TLS/MQTT**
- Listens for commands on `data/terminal/input`
- Runs them in a **persistent `/bin/sh` session** (so `cd`, `export`, etc. work correctly across commands)
- Publishes output back on `data/terminal/output` as JSON
- Blocks dangerous commands (`rm -rf /`, `mkfs`, fork bombs)
- Runs as a **systemd service** — starts automatically on boot

### Persistent shell architecture

Each command runs inside one long-lived shell process, not a new one each time:

```
Agent process            /bin/sh (persistent)
    │                         │
    ├── write "cd /tmp\n" ──► │  shell changes directory
    ├── write "echo END" ───► │  sentinel marks end of output
    ├── read until sentinel ◄─┤
    │                         │
    ├── write "ls\n" ───────► │  ls runs in /tmp  ✓
    └── read output ◄─────────┘
```

### Dependencies
None needed on the board — the binary is **fully statically linked**.

Only one file must exist on the board:
```
/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt
```

### Cross-compile in WSL

**1. One-time setup:**
```bash
# Get bundled cJSON
wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DaveGamble/cJSON/master/cJSON.c
wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DaveGamble/cJSON/master/cJSON.h

# Install ARM toolchain and libs
sudo dpkg --add-architecture armhf
sudo apt update
sudo apt install gcc-arm-linux-gnueabihf libssl-dev:armhf

# Build mosquitto static lib from source
wget https://mosquitto.org/files/source/mosquitto-2.0.18.tar.gz
tar xf mosquitto-2.0.18.tar.gz && cd mosquitto-2.0.18
cmake -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=arm-linux-gnueabihf-gcc \
      -DCMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=Linux \
      -DWITH_STATIC_LIBRARIES=ON \
      -DWITH_SHARED_LIBRARIES=OFF \
      -DWITH_CLIENTS=OFF -DWITH_BROKER=OFF \
      -DWITH_APPS=OFF -DDOCUMENTATION=OFF .
make -j$(nproc)
cd ..
```

**2. Compile:**
```bash
arm-linux-gnueabihf-gcc -o pi_terminal_agent \
    pi_terminal_agent.c cJSON.c \
    -I. \
    -I mosquitto-2.0.18/include \
    -static \
    mosquitto-2.0.18/lib/libmosquitto_static.a \
    -lssl -lcrypto -lpthread -ldl \
    -march=armv7-a -mfpu=neon-vfpv4 -mfloat-abi=hard
```

**3. Verify:**
```bash
file pi_terminal_agent
# ELF 32-bit LSB executable, ARM, statically linked  ✓
```

**4. Transfer to board:**
```bash
# Copy CA cert (one-time)
scp /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt root@<board-ip>:/etc/ssl/certs/

# Copy binary
scp pi_terminal_agent root@<board-ip>:/home/root/edb_c/mqtt_terminal/
```

### Install as systemd service

On the board:

```bash
nano /etc/systemd/system/mqtt-terminal.service
```

```ini
[Unit]
Description=MQTT Terminal Agent
After=network.target

[Service]
ExecStartPre=/bin/sleep 10
ExecStart=/home/root/edb_c/mqtt_terminal/pi_terminal_agent
Restart=always
RestartSec=5
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```

```bash
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl enable mqtt-terminal
systemctl start mqtt-terminal
```

**Useful service commands:**
```bash
systemctl status mqtt-terminal     # check status
journalctl -fu mqtt-terminal       # live logs
systemctl restart mqtt-terminal    # restart after update
```

---

## PC Client (`mqtt_terminal.py`)

### What it does
- Connects to the same HiveMQ broker over TLS
- Presents a colored terminal prompt: `root@stm32mp1:~#`
- Sends commands to the board and waits for the response before showing the next prompt
- Auto-reconnects if the broker drops
- Supports command history (↑ ↓ arrow keys)

### Install

```bash
pip install paho-mqtt pyreadline3   # pyreadline3 needed on Windows
```

### Run

```bash
python mqtt_terminal.py
```

### Terminal appearance

```
  ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
  ║         MQTT  REMOTE  TERMINAL  CLIENT               ║
  ║         Target : stm32mp1                            ║
  ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

  ●  Board online  [2026-05-30 09:28:33]

root@stm32mp1:~# ls
── 2026-05-30 09:28:35 ──────────────────────────────
  edb_c
  ipc_test
  ipc_test.c

root@stm32mp1:~# cd edb_c
── 2026-05-30 09:28:37 ──────────────────────────────
  (no output)

root@stm32mp1:~#
```

### Local commands

| Command | Action |
|---------|--------|
| `clear` | Clear the screen |
| `exit` / `quit` | Disconnect and quit |
| `help` | Show help |
| ↑ / ↓ | Navigate command history |

All other commands are sent to the board.

---

## MQTT Topics

| Topic | Direction | Description |
|-------|-----------|-------------|
| `data/terminal/input` | PC → Board | Command to run |
| `data/terminal/output` | Board → PC | Command output |

### Message format

**Input (PC → Board):**
```json
{ "cmd": "ls -la" }
```

**Output (Board → PC):**
```json
{
  "type": "output",
  "command": "ls -la",
  "output": "total 32\ndrwxr-xr-x ...",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-30 09:28:35"
}
```

**Status:**
```json
{
  "type": "status",
  "message": "STM32MP1 terminal online",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-30 09:28:33"
}
```

---

## Configuration

Both files share the same broker config — edit at the top of each file:

```c
// pi_terminal_agent.c
#define MQTT_BROKER   "your-broker.hivemq.cloud"
#define MQTT_PORT     8883
#define MQTT_USERNAME "username"
#define MQTT_PASSWORD "password"
```

```python
# mqtt_terminal.py
MQTT_BROKER   = 'your-broker.hivemq.cloud'
MQTT_PORT     = 8883
MQTT_USERNAME = 'username'
MQTT_PASSWORD = 'password'
```

---

## Blocked Commands

The agent refuses the following for safety:

- `rm -rf /`
- `mkfs`
- `:(){ :|:& };:` (fork bomb)

To add more, edit the `BLOCKED` array in `pi_terminal_agent.c` and recompile.

---

## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| `TLS setup failed` | Check `/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt` exists on board |
| `No response from board` | Check service is running: `systemctl status mqtt-terminal` |
| `cd` not working | Use absolute paths or `cd /path && ls` in one command |
| Service not starting on boot | Check `ExecStart` path matches binary location |
| Binary runs as text file | Recompile — the `.c` source was copied instead of the binary |
| `ModuleNotFoundError: readline` | Run `pip install pyreadline3` on Windows |